# Three.js scenes and animation

- Follow the existing React Three Fiber and Drei patterns. Access Three.js objects through refs and Fiber hooks rather than manipulating the DOM.
- Preserve the three-scene order and the matching camera and planet values in `src/data/scenesData.js`.
- Scene direction is shared by pointer and touch navigation. Keep back/next behavior consistent on both inputs.
- Treat GSAP timelines as lifecycle-bound resources: stop or clean up timelines when their scene changes or their component unmounts, and avoid competing tweens on the same transform.
- When changing an animated model's transform, account for its parent group and the model's own initial rotation; verify the final position and facing direction, not just that the animation compiles.
- Keep public 3D assets referenced consistently with the existing `/airplane.gltf` and `/planet.gltf` paths.
- Do not change generated model geometry or asset licensing headers as part of unrelated animation work.
